Fillets: where none of the samples along the spine finds a start as an edge
overflow, the spine is sampled four times as finely between them
(mitcad#343).

The case: 0904's notch wall on the other side of the bar's end, rounded
with 0.86 along a spine of two edges 17.7 long, whose ball touches an
earlier rounding and rolls on the wall's far edge. StartSolOverflow
samples the spine at eleven points (1.6 to 1.8 apart). A start is found
only where the wall's side, crossing its far edge, reaches the face it
rolls before and the other side's contact lies inside its face: a stretch
of about a millimetre. On the stored body one sample fell in it; on a body
a few micrometres off, parametrised a little differently, none did, and
the stripe failed ("no ball of the radius touches both faces there").

- StartSolOverflow: the samples first as before, then those between them
  at a quarter of their spacing, until one finds a start.

Upstream: new.

